</div></div><div class="vc_tta-panel" id="1476008685437-e551bbc8-00af" data-vc-content=".vc_tta-panel-body"><div class="vc_tta-panel-heading"><h4 class="vc_tta-panel-title"><a href="sarah@cet.ac.il#1476008685437-e551bbc8-00af" data-vc-accordion data-vc-container=".vc_tta-container"><span class="vc_tta-title-text">Conference Poster</span></a></h4></div><div class="vc_tta-panel-body">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p dir="ltr"><span style="color: #000000; font-size: 18px;"> The <a href="http://www.jct.ac.il/sites/default/files/poster%20ACA%202017%20-%20landscape%20%282%29.pdf">conference poster</a> is now downloadable. You are cordially invited to download it and to dispatch it to people/departments to whom you wish to advertise the conference.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</article>
</div>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div><div class="vc_tta-panel" id="1476008686173-9936ffa3-717f" data-vc-content=".vc_tta-panel-body"><div class="vc_tta-panel-heading"><h4 class="vc_tta-panel-title"><a href="sarah@cet.ac.il#1476008686173-9936ffa3-717f" data-vc-accordion data-vc-container=".vc_tta-container"><span class="vc_tta-title-text">Publications</span></a></h4></div><div class="vc_tta-panel-body">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<div>
<article id="fl-post-5">
<div data-post-id="5">
<div data-node="57ebc7eba8b41">
<div data-node="57ebc7eba979e">
<div data-node="57ebc7eba9900">
<div data-node="57ebc7eba89c8" data-animation-delay="0.0">
<div data-index="11">
<div id="main">
<div id="block-system-main">
<div dir="rtl">
<p style="text-align: left;"><strong>BOOK OF ABSTRACTS</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 18px;">If you are interested in proposing a talk, please send an abstract to the organizers of the suitable session</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 18px;">Please use this LaTeX template for your abstract and send both the LaTeX source and a compiled PDF version</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 18px;">.(The <a href="http://homedir.jct.ac.il/~naiman/aca2017/abstracts.pdf">book of abstracts</a> is downloadable <a href="http://homedir.jct.ac.il/~naiman/aca2017/abstracts.pdf">here</a> (pdf file</span></p>
<h4 style="text-align: left;"><strong>PROCEEDINGS</strong></h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left; padding-right: 30px;"><span style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 18px;">.We plan to publish proceedings of ACA 2017 as a special issue of the journal <a href="http://link.springer.com/journal/11786" target="_blank">Mathematics in Computer Science</a>. Details will be announced ASAP</span></h4>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</article>
</div>
<footer style="padding-left: 30px;"></footer>
<p><img class="alignnone wp-image-213" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Cover_of_MCS-p1bb8p5jjaunf1f9u41c1d5s1uvg.png" alt="Cover_of_MCS-p1bb8p5jjaunf1f9u41c1d5s1uvg" width="338" height="454" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Cover_of_MCS-p1bb8p5jjaunf1f9u41c1d5s1uvg.png 827w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Cover_of_MCS-p1bb8p5jjaunf1f9u41c1d5s1uvg-223x300.png 223w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Cover_of_MCS-p1bb8p5jjaunf1f9u41c1d5s1uvg-768x1032.png 768w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Cover_of_MCS-p1bb8p5jjaunf1f9u41c1d5s1uvg-762x1024.png 762w" sizes="(max-width: 338px) 100vw, 338px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img class="alignnone wp-image-405" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Call-for-Papers-211x300.jpg" alt="Call for Papers" width="338" height="479" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Call-for-Papers-211x300.jpg 211w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Call-for-Papers-768x1089.jpg 768w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Call-for-Papers-722x1024.jpg 722w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Call-for-Papers.jpg 1572w" sizes="(max-width: 338px) 100vw, 338px" /></p>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div><div class="vc_tta-panel" id="1476008686938-950eaea7-54e9" data-vc-content=".vc_tta-panel-body"><div class="vc_tta-panel-heading"><h4 class="vc_tta-panel-title"><a href="sarah@cet.ac.il#1476008686938-950eaea7-54e9" data-vc-accordion data-vc-container=".vc_tta-container"><span class="vc_tta-title-text">Location</span></a></h4></div><div class="vc_tta-panel-body">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<h4 dir="ltr">The conference will take place on the Lev Campus of Jerusalem College of Technology (Lev Academic Center).</h4>
<h4 dir="ltr">The campus is located at 21, Havaad Haleumi Street, Jerusalem, in the Givat Mordechai area. It is close to the Begin Road and can be easily reached by public transportation.</h4>
<h4 dir="ltr"><strong>Transportation:</strong> Bus: 5,6,9,39</h4>
<h4 dir="ltr"><strong>Tramway</strong>: Shaare Tsedek Hospital station, then cross the road and take bus 39 to Givat Mordechai.</h4>
<h4 dir="ltr"><strong>Taxis</strong>: they have a yellow sign on their roof with a registration number. You can stop a taxi on the street, or find taxi stations in every part of Jerusalem. Some companies have a mobile application (for example Gett).</h4>
<h4 dir="ltr">For participants coming with a car, there is a parking lot at the entrance of the campus. On the campus, the parking facilities are quite limited. In the immediate neighbourhood of the workshop venue is a cafeteria open all day long. There are also vending machines at various places of the campus for snacks and refreshments.</h4>
<h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: center;"><span style="color: #0000ff;"><strong><a style="color: #0000ff;" href="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/10/lev-campus-new-map.pdf">lev campus new map</a></strong></span></h3>
<p><img class="aligncenter wp-image-24 size-full" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/10/Route-to-JCT.jpg" alt="route-to-jct" width="519" height="507" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/Route-to-JCT.jpg 519w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/Route-to-JCT-300x293.jpg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 519px) 100vw, 519px" /></p>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div><div class="vc_tta-panel" id="1476008687720-c496ac02-8506" data-vc-content=".vc_tta-panel-body"><div class="vc_tta-panel-heading"><h4 class="vc_tta-panel-title"><a href="sarah@cet.ac.il#1476008687720-c496ac02-8506" data-vc-accordion data-vc-container=".vc_tta-container"><span class="vc_tta-title-text">Social Program</span></a></h4></div><div class="vc_tta-panel-body">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<h2>CONFERENCE EXCURSION</h2>
<p><strong>We are offering registered participants and registered accompanying persons a conference excursion to interesting places in Jerusalem, </strong></p>
<p><strong>The excursion is planned on Wednesday afternoon, July 19th. It is supported by the  Authority for Jerusalem Development. </strong></p>
<p><strong>Buses will collect the participants from JCT Lev campus after lunch, to the City of David. There we will have an overview on 3000 years of history of the Holy City. </strong></p>
<h2>CONFERENCE DINNER</h2>
<p><strong>After the excursion, buses will take us to the Bayit Vegan area, across the street of Mount Hertzl. Participants who wish to have a short walk can enjoy the park there and a nice view over Jerusalem Hills.</strong></p>
<p><strong> The conference dinner will take place in the nice Social Hall of the Bayit Vegan Guest House.</strong></p>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div><div class="vc_tta-panel" id="1476008688485-0daf753e-13ca" data-vc-content=".vc_tta-panel-body"><div class="vc_tta-panel-heading"><h4 class="vc_tta-panel-title"><a href="sarah@cet.ac.il#1476008688485-0daf753e-13ca" data-vc-accordion data-vc-container=".vc_tta-container"><span class="vc_tta-title-text">Travel</span></a></h4></div><div class="vc_tta-panel-body">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<article id="fl-post-5">
<div data-post-id="5">
<div data-node="57ebc7eba8b41">
<div data-node="57ebc7eba979e">
<div data-node="57ebc7eba9900">
<div data-node="57ebc7eba89c8" data-animation-delay="0.0">
<div data-index="14">
<div id="main">
<div id="block-system-main">
<div dir="rtl">
<footer id="footer">
<div id="mini-panel-footer">
<h4 style="text-align: left;"><strong>Airport</strong></h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left;">.Israel’s international airport is <span style="color: #0000ff;"><a style="color: #0000ff;" href="http://www.iaa.gov.il/en-US/airports/bengurion/Pages/default.aspx">Ben Gurion Airport</a></span>, in the Tel Aviv area (code TLV)</h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left;">.General info for arriving travelers may be found <span style="color: #0000ff;"><a style="color: #0000ff;" href="http://www.iaa.gov.il/en-US/airports/bengurion/Pages/ArrivingPassengers.aspx">here</a></span></h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left;">The easiest way to travel from the airport to Jerusalem is using shuttle taxis (<span style="color: #0000ff;"><a style="color: #0000ff;" href="http://www.neshertours.co.il/taxis-from-ben-gurion">Nesher company</a></span>; phone number for enquiries: 02-6222553, 02-6257227). The taxi station and dispatcher post are located in front of the Terminal on Level G (arrivals), near the exit through Gate 01.They have a flat fare policy (see the company’s website), no matter to which hotel you wish to arrive in Jerusalem</h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left;">.You may use also a special taxi, which can be ordered prior your trip or upon arrival. See info on the airport’s website</h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left;"><strong>Visa</strong></h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left;">Israel has exemption agreements with dozens of countries, but some participants may need a visa to enter Israel. Please inform yourself at an Israeli embassy/consulate about the precise procedure and take into account that visa applications typically require quite some time to be processed. You may consult the suitable page on the website of the <span style="color: #0000ff;"><a style="color: #0000ff;" href="http://mfa.gov.il/MFA/ConsularServices/Pages/Visas.aspx">Ministry of Foreign Affairs</a></span>. in particular the <a href="http://mfa.gov.il/MFA/ConsularServices/Documents/VisaRequirements-Tourists.pdf">interactive page</a> for checking whether you need a visa or not. Here is the Ministry’s webpage which can help you to find if there are <span style="color: #0000ff;"><a style="color: #0000ff;" href="http://mfa.gov.il/MFA/ConsularServices/Pages/default.aspx">Israeli consular services</a></span> in your country</h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left;">If your country has no Israeli diplomatic representation, your travel agent should know the procedure for applying for a visa</h4>
<h4 style="text-align: left;">If you need a letter of invitation, write after your registration an e-mail to the <span style="color: #0000ff;"><a style="color: #0000ff;" href="mailto:aca2017-organizers@jct.ac.il">organizing committee</a></span> containing your full name and the address to which the letter should be sent (we send letters only to your private or work address, not directly to embassies or consulates). If you plan to give a talk, then also include the title of your talk. We will then send you the letter by mail and a scan of the letter by e-mail. Please understand that we can provide letters of invitation only for registered participants</h4>
</div>
</footer>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</article>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div><div class="vc_tta-panel" id="1476008689252-685cae24-5dc2" data-vc-content=".vc_tta-panel-body"><div class="vc_tta-panel-heading"><h4 class="vc_tta-panel-title"><a href="sarah@cet.ac.il#1476008689252-685cae24-5dc2" data-vc-accordion data-vc-container=".vc_tta-container"><span class="vc_tta-title-text">Accommodation</span></a></h4></div><div class="vc_tta-panel-body">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<div>
<p><strong>Accommodation</strong></p>
<p><img class="alignnone wp-image-147 size-large" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1-1024x200.jpg" alt="1" width="1024" height="200" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1-1024x200.jpg 1024w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1-300x59.jpg 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1-768x150.jpg 768w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/1.jpg 1269w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p>
</div>
<h4><strong>There are numerous hotels, hostels, albergos, etc. in Jerusalem.</strong></h4>
<h4><a href="https://www.itraveljerusalem.com/hotels/"><strong>Here</strong></a><strong> is a website where the hotels are classified according to various criteria: star number, location, etc.  </strong></h4>
<h4><strong>Here are the areas we suggest you to choose:</strong></h4>
<ol>
<li>
<h4><strong>Central Bus Station Mall (the central bus station is not in city center, this is a name for the intercity main bus station) <em>(Tramway stop: Central Station)</em></strong></h4>
</li>
<li>
<h4><strong>West Jerusalem (probably the closest to the campus are listed there): Ramada, Jerusalem Gardens Hotel and Spa, Prima Park are on the same street (Vilani St.). <em>Tramway stop: Kiryat Moshe (Ben Dor)</em></strong></h4>
</li>
<li>
<h4><strong>Jaffa Street area.</strong></h4>
</li>
<li>
<h4><strong>City Center <em>(Tramway stop: Jaffa Center)</em></strong></h4>
</li>
<li>
<h4><strong>Machane Yehuda stop Market <em>(Tramway: Mahane Yehuda)</em></strong></h4>
</li>
</ol>
<h4><img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-148" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2-1024x493.png" alt="2" width="1024" height="493" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2-1024x493.png 1024w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2-300x144.png 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2-768x370.png 768w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/2.png 1275w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></h4>
<h4><strong>The closest hotel is <a href="http://www.rimonimhotels.com/rimonim-jerusalem">Rimonim Shalom</a>. On foot, via a "trail", it takes 5-7 minutes to the campus. With a taxi, it takes 5-8 minutes.</strong></h4>
<h4><strong>1-2: From there you arrive to the campus entrance by bus no 6 (3 stops).</strong></h4>
<h4><strong>3-4-5: you arrive to the campus with bus 19 or with the Tramway (until stop Yefe Nof) and then bus 5, 39 (it will take about 25 minutes, depending on the period).</strong></h4>
<h4><strong>There are also good hotels close to Old City, but at a greater distance from the campus. <em>Tramway stops: Shivtei Israel, Shimon Hatsadik.</em></strong></h4>
<h4><strong><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-153" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Presentation1.jpg" alt="Presentation1" width="960" height="720" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Presentation1.jpg 960w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Presentation1-300x225.jpg 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Presentation1-768x576.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px" /></strong></h4>
<h4><strong>The black arrow shows the direction to the campus.</strong></h4>
<h4><strong> </strong></h4>
<h4><strong>Some hotels are listed in more than one area, as these areas are not disconnected open sets.</strong></h4>
<h4><strong>Of course you may use the classical sites such as </strong><a href="http://www.booking.com/Jerusalem/Hotels‎"><strong>booking.com</strong></a><strong>, </strong><a href="http://www.trivago.com/Hotel‎"><strong>trivago.com</strong></a><strong>, </strong><a href="http://www.hotels.com/Jerusalem/Hotels"><strong>hotels.com</strong></a><strong>, etc. The first one has a special subsite </strong><a href="http://www.booking.com/Jerusalem/Cheap-Hotels‎"><strong>for cheap hotels</strong></a><strong> in Jerusalem.</strong></h4>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div><div class="vc_tta-panel" id="1483435292557-902b9509-6e81" data-vc-content=".vc_tta-panel-body"><div class="vc_tta-panel-heading"><h4 class="vc_tta-panel-title"><a href="sarah@cet.ac.il#1483435292557-902b9509-6e81" data-vc-accordion data-vc-container=".vc_tta-container"><span class="vc_tta-title-text">Sponsors</span></a></h4></div><div class="vc_tta-panel-body">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p><a href="../../../../../index.html?p=351" rel="attachment wp-att-351"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-351" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image001-1-300x182.png" alt="image001" width="300" height="182" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image001-1-300x182.png 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image001-1.png 312w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></a></p>
<p><a href="http://www.home.cet.ac.il/"><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-126" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/image001.png" alt="image001" width="224" height="81" /></a> Center for Educational Technology (CET), Tel Aviv</p>
<p><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-92" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2017/01/wolfram.png" alt="wolfram" width="240" height="70" />   <a href="../../../../../index.html?p=209" target="_blank"><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-99" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/maplesoft.png" alt="maplesoft" width="188" height="70" /></a></p>
<p><a href="http://www.cargo.wlu.ca/" target="_blank"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-91" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2017/01/cargo-300x68.jpg" alt="cargo" width="300" height="68" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/cargo-300x68.jpg 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/cargo.jpg 576w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.wlu.ca"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-124" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Laurier-300x88.png" alt="Laurier" width="300" height="88" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Laurier-300x88.png 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/Laurier.png 457w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></a> Wilfrid Laurier University, ON, Canada</p>
<p><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-129" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/�%2594�%2590�%2592�%2595�%2593-�%2594�%2599שר�%2590�%259C�%2599-�%259C�%259Eת�%259E�%2598�%2599ק�%2594-300x143.jpg" alt="האגוד הישראלי למתמטיקה" width="300" height="143" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/האגוד-הישראלי-למתמטיקה-300x143.jpg 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/האגוד-הישראלי-למתמטיקה.jpg 476w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></p>
<p><a href="https://carma.newcastle.edu.au/" target="_blank"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-168" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2016/09/carma_logo-300x75.jpg" alt="carma_logo" width="300" height="75" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/carma_logo-300x75.jpg 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/carma_logo-768x192.jpg 768w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/carma_logo-1024x257.jpg 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></a>COMPUTER-ASSISTED RESEARCH MATHEMATICS AND ITS APPLICATIONS</p>
<p><a href="http://u.cs.biu.ac.il/~eni/" target="_blank"><img class="alignnone wp-image-185" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Emmy-Noether-300x132.jpg" alt="Emmy Noether" width="318" height="140" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Emmy-Noether-300x132.jpg 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Emmy-Noether.jpg 386w" sizes="(max-width: 318px) 100vw, 318px" /></a></p>
<p><a href="http://www.cs.technion.ac.il/~cggc" target="_blank"><img class="alignnone wp-image-186" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2017/03/iconxlnt-CGGC-300x97.jpg" alt="iconxlnt-CGGC" width="331" height="107" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/iconxlnt-CGGC-300x97.jpg 300w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/iconxlnt-CGGC-768x248.jpg 768w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/iconxlnt-CGGC-1024x330.jpg 1024w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/iconxlnt-CGGC.jpg 1370w" sizes="(max-width: 331px) 100vw, 331px" /></a></p>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div><div class="vc_tta-panel" id="1484645131083-fd1b9173-4617" data-vc-content=".vc_tta-panel-body"><div class="vc_tta-panel-heading"><h4 class="vc_tta-panel-title"><a href="sarah@cet.ac.il#1484645131083-fd1b9173-4617" data-vc-accordion data-vc-container=".vc_tta-container"><span class="vc_tta-title-text">Jonathan Borwein</span></a></h4></div><div class="vc_tta-panel-body">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<h3><span style="color: #000000;"><strong>Jonatan Borwein </strong><strong>ז"ל</strong></span></h3>
<p><span style="color: #000000;">Very few mathematicians manage to transcend the boundaries of more than one mathematical discipline and make substantial contributions to several areas of Mathematics. Jon was undeniably one of them. He was a paragon of Experimental Mathematics, Symbolic Computation, Functional Analysis, Optimization and other areas. His research work has already inspired thousands of individual researchers and will remain as a testament to this generation and to the coming ones.</span></p>
<p><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-108" src="../../../../../wp-content/uploads/2017/01/jonathan-276x300.png" alt="jonathan" width="276" height="300" srcset="http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/jonathan-276x300.png 276w, http://www.aca2017.jct.ac.il/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/jonathan.png 340w" sizes="(max-width: 276px) 100vw, 276px" /></p>
<p><a href="https://cms.math.ca/MediaReleases/2016/borweinobituary">https://cms.math.ca/MediaReleases/2016/borweinobituary</a></p>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
